From d311a8d04ecdeec27c06ddeff3575ec62176cf67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:44:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] p60: GGML_CUDA_P60_INVAR - MTP output identical to
 plain decode

With the fast persistent kernels (GGML_CUDA_P60_MMVQ=1, MEGA=1) the
multi-token verify kernels (p60-mega-t.cu, p60-fa.cu, q8_0_t) already
give bit-identical per-token results for T = 2..6, but single-token
decode used the fp32 single-token kernels (p60-mega.cu, mmvq-p60), so a
token's logits depended on whether it was verified in a batch or
decoded alone. GGML_CUDA_P60_INVAR=1 runs single-token steps through
the multi-token kernels with T = 1 (MoE half, gated delta net half,
q8_0 output layer; the attention half already used one kernel family).

Measured (greedy, 3 real harness prompts): logits of T=1..6 bit-
identical over 160 rows incl. a 256-position KV boundary; llama-server
with MTP gives token-identical output to the same build without MTP.
Speed with MTP 153/250/200 -> 149/225/197 t/s, without MTP ~ -1%.
Also adds debug dumps (GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGAT_DUMP) to the gdn / moe
multi-token launchers.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
